  steps:['Open Redact PDF and add your file.','Drag a rectangle over each area to hide; page through the document and repeat.','Select Cover areas & download, then save the redacted PDF.'],
  know:['This is true redaction: covered text is removed from the file, not just hidden under a black shape.','Pages without boxes are copied across unchanged, with their text intact.'],
  faqs:[
    {q:'Is it free to redact a PDF here?',a:'Yes — completely free, no account, no watermark.'},
    {q:'Is the hidden text really gone?',a:'Yes. Redacted pages are rebuilt as images with the boxes burned in — there is no text layer left to copy from those areas.'},
    {q:'Are my files uploaded?',a:'No. Redaction happens in your browser — exactly where sensitive documents belong.'},
    {q:'Should I keep the original?',a:'Yes — redaction cannot be undone. Keep your unredacted original somewhere safe and private.'}],
